		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4The Wither is less a creature and more a calamity given form, a floating tangle of skulls and black energy that rots the land as it drifts. We’ve seen its handiwork: craters, twisted trees, and a sky choked with ash where once there was sunlight. Its projectiles don’t just wound, they linger, gnawing at life and hope alike. If we summon it, there will be no turning back; we’ll either stand together long enough to bring it down, or leave behind another scar on the world."]
			id: "72EA62835F4AEFD9"
			size: 1.15d
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "minecraft:nether/summon_wither"
				criterion: ""
				icon: "minecraft:wither_rose"
				id: "42306210AEE8D040"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			x: 0.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4We arrived to the sound of bells and screams, pillager banners flapping crimson over fields trampled by ravagers. Crossbow bolts thudded into walls as iron golems roared and threw raiders into the air like rag dolls. Fighting in the cramped streets, dodging panicked villagers and stray arrows, felt more like chaos than heroism. But when the last horn blew and the survivors came out with gifts and shy smiles, it felt like, for once, we’d actually made the world a little better."]
			id: "443D68F7812B0BD5"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "minecraft:adventure/hero_of_the_village"
				criterion: ""
				id: "1267B0022514FD99"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			x: 1.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4The Bonescaller stands in graveyards like a shepherd, staff tapping softly as skeletons claw their way from the dirt at his command. He doesn’t shout or rage; he murmurs, and the dead obey. We saw him once at a distance, silhouettes rising behind him like a forest of bone, each skull turning in perfect unison. Killing him won’t just be a matter of steel, it will mean wading through his pale congregation while he tears at our courage with whispered curses."]
			id: "4D814D7620E3E98E"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "born_in_chaos_v1:junior_summoner"
				criterion: ""
				id: "7FE956C8701781B4"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			x: -1.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4If the Bonescaller is a shepherd, the Supreme Bonescaller is a high priest of death itself. Wherever he walks, the world goes quiet: candle flames gutter, animals flee, and even the air feels thin and cold. He doesn’t just raise skeletons; he bends entire battlefields of the fallen to his will, weaving them into disciplined ranks. Facing him will be like fighting a whole forgotten war at once, soldiers of every age and armor clattering forward under one terrible mind."]
			id: "2D597F553C8571B1"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "born_in_chaos_v1:dismantledto_bones"
				criterion: ""
				id: "0FE68674F266CF4D"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			x: -2.5d
			y: -0.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4The Glutton Fish lurks in waters that should be too small to hold something that big, yet somehow do. We watched it swallow a cow that strayed too close to the riverbank, the water barely rippling as rows of jagged teeth snapped shut. Its bulk moves with a horrible, lazy grace, drawn to splashing and blood like a living whirlpool. To face it, we’ll have to fight the urge to panic whenever it vanishes below, knowing it could surge up beneath us at any moment."]
			icon: "born_in_chaos_v1:sea_terror_eye"
			id: "384C10251DACEE34"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "born_in_chaos_v1:glutton_fish"
				id: "12C22F09893543F1"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			x: -2.5d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4We first heard the chittering long before we saw her, a slow, echoing sound that seemed to crawl under our skin. The Mother of Spider sits at the heart of her nest like a bloated jewel, surrounded by webs so thick they muffle sound and swallow light. When she moves, the whole cavern shifts with her, and lesser spiders spill from the ceiling like black rain. If we face her, we’ll need fire and sharp blades, and nerves steady enough not to bolt when the eggs start hatching."]
			icon: "born_in_chaos_v1:spider_mandible"
			id: "55B97B5BE5ED5021"
