				}
				id: "09CBEA18B379E97F"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			x: 4.0d
			y: -0.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4The Ancient Knight stands watch where the world has forgotten the reason for the watch in the first place. Moss creeps over his armor, and yet every movement he makes is crisp, practiced, and utterly relentless. He doesn’t taunt or rage; he simply tests us, blow after blow, as if measuring us against some old, impossible standard. If we can best him, it won’t feel like a victory over evil—more like earning the respect of a guardian who was never meant to yield."]
			id: "7CDFBC158801FAF9"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "irons_spellbooks:citadel_keeper"
				icon: "irons_spellbooks:armor_pile"
				id: "1293E604EB1D4976"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			x: 5.5d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["30784E3952DDFD84"]
			description: ["&4The Dead King rules a kingdom of dust and silence, seated on a throne of cracked stone and rusted crowns. His armor is ancient, but death has made him patient and terribly strong; every blow he takes rings like a funeral bell. Around him, ghostly knights repeat their last charges, spectral lines of cavalry breaking and reforming in endless loops. To end his reign, we’ll have to break the pattern—shatter the ritual of his unlife and topple the throne that keeps him from rest."]
			id: "0C0E8CD401D8DF87"
			size: 1.15d
			tasks: [{
				entity: "irons_spellbooks:dead_king"
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "irons_spellbooks:gold_crown"
					tag: {
						Damage: 0
					}
				}
				id: "624929FC33F50FD1"
